abstract: >-
  Cohort-definition and analysis code, together with all aggregate outputs, for a
  study that defined and externally replicated a bedside congestion–perfusion
  phenotype (nurse-charted pitting oedema depth and capillary refill time) in
  20,806 first cardiac intensive care unit stays in MIMIC-IV v3.1, with
  replication in the eICU Collaborative Research Database v2.0. No row-level
  patient data are included: the PhysioNet data use agreements for both
  databases prohibit redistribution of patient-level records.
